 "grammar": {
  "g.L10.loc": {
   "id": "g.L10.loc",
   "title": "Locative -DA: in / at / on",
   "suffixes": [
    "sfx.loc"
   ],
   "reference": "**-DA** means *in*, *at* or *on*: **ev·de** \"at home\", **masa·da** \"on the table\", **çanta·da** \"in the bag\".\n\n**Vowel (A):** look at the *last* vowel of the word.\na ı o u → **-da** · e i ö ü → **-de**\n\n**Consonant (D):** after one of the voiceless consonants **f s t k ç ş h p** (\"**F**ı**st**ı**kç**ı **Ş**a**h**a**p**\") → **-ta / -te**; otherwise **-da / -de**.\n\nThe word itself never changes before -DA: *kitap → kitapta*, *mutfak → mutfakta*.\nAfter a plural: **ev·ler·de** \"in the houses\".\n",
   "patterns": [
    {
     "id": "g.L10.loc.back",
     "description": "Back last vowel → -da",
     "suffix": "sfx.loc",
     "word_filter": {
      "pos": "noun",
      "last_vowel": "back",
      "ends_with": "voiced_consonant"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "g.L10.loc.front",
     "description": "Front last vowel → -de",
     "suffix": "sfx.loc",
     "word_filter": {
      "pos": "noun",
      "last_vowel": "front",
      "ends_with": "voiced_consonant"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "g.L10.loc.after_vowel",
     "description": "Word ends in a vowel → d",
     "suffix": "sfx.loc",
     "word_filter": {
      "pos": "noun",
      "ends_with": "vowel"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "g.L10.loc.voiceless",
     "description": "Ends in f s t k ç ş h p → -ta / -te",
     "suffix": "sfx.loc",
     "word_filter": {
      "pos": "noun",
      "ends_with": "voiceless"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "g.L10.loc.last_vowel",
     "description": "First and last vowels differ in harmony: only the last one counts",
     "suffix": "sfx.loc",
     "word_filter": {
      "pos": "noun",
      "last_vowel_differs_from_first": true
     }
    }
   ],
   "feedback": {
    "vowel_back": "Look at the last vowel of **{word}**: **{v}** is a back vowel (a ı o u) → **-{D}a**.",
    "vowel_front": "Look at the last vowel of **{word}**: **{v}** is a front vowel (e i ö ü) → **-{D}e**.",
    "last_not_first": "Only the **last** vowel counts, not the first one.",
    "voiceless": "**{word}** ends in **{c}**, one of the Fıstıkçı Şahap letters → **t**: {answer}.",
    "not_voiceless": "**{c}** is not in Fıstıkçı Şahap → **d**: {answer}.",
    "after_vowel": "**{word}** ends in a vowel → always **d**: {answer}.",
    "detached": "The location ending is **attached** to the word: **{answer}**.",
    "stem_changed": "-DA starts with a consonant, so **{word}** doesn't change: **{answer}**.",
    "accent": "Almost! **{expected_letter}**, not {given_letter}: **{answer}**."
   }
  }
 },
 "lessons": {
  "L10": {
   "id": "L10",
   "title": "Locative -DA: in / at / on",
   "grammar": "g.L10.loc",
   "new_words": [
    "w.burada",
    "w.orada"
   ],
   "not_yet": [
    "personal endings on the location (evdeyim) → L11",
    "apostrophes on names (İstanbul'da) → L11",
    "the separate word de 'too' → L13"
   ],
   "sessions": {
    "learn": {
     "minutes": 3.5,
     "cards": [
      {
       "kind": "hook",
       "body": "🐈 **Kedi nerede?** \"Where is the cat?\"\n🛋️ **Kedi kanepede.** \"The cat is on the sofa.\"\n\nTurkish doesn't say *on the sofa*. It adds an ending to the word: **kanepe → kanepe·de**.\n",
       "sentences": [
        "s.L10.001",
        "s.L10.002"
       ],
       "audio": [
        "aud.own.s.L10.001",
        "aud.own.s.L10.002"
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "rule",
       "title": "Meaning: in, at, on",
       "body": "**-DA = in, at, on**. One ending covers all three English prepositions.\n\n| Turkish | English |\n|---|---|\n| ev·**de** | **at** home / **in** the house |\n| masa·**da** | **on** the table |\n| çanta·**da** | **in** the bag |\n\n💡 There's no \"is\" in *Kedi kanepede*. As in L3, the 3rd person needs no verb \"to be\".\n"
      },
      {
       "kind": "rule",
       "title": "The vowel: a or e?",
       "body": "The **A** in -DA follows 2-way harmony. Look at the **last vowel** of the word:\n\n| Last vowel | Ending | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| a ı o u (back) | **-da** | oda·da, okul·da, banyo·da |\n| e i ö ü (front) | **-de** | ev·de, bahçe·de, pencere·de |\n\n⚠️ Only the **last** vowel counts: o·to·**bü**s → front → otobüs·**te** (not ~~otobüsta~~).\n",
       "interactive": {
        "component": "vowel_chart_tap",
        "params": {
         "words": [
          "w.otobüs",
          "w.kanepe",
          "w.okul"
         ]
        }
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "rule",
       "title": "The consonant: d or t?",
       "body": "The **D** in -DA becomes **t** after a *voiceless* consonant. There are only 8 of them:\n\n**F**ı**st**ı**kç**ı **Ş**a**h**a**p** — \"Şahap the pistachio seller\" → **f s t k ç ş h p**\n\n| Word ends in… | Ending | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| a vowel | -da / -de | masa·da, kanepe·de |\n| another consonant | -da / -de | okul·da, ev·de |\n| f s t k ç ş h p | **-ta / -te** | kitap·**ta**, mutfak·**ta**, süt·**te**, otobüs·**te** |\n\n✅ -DA starts with a consonant, so **the word itself never changes**: *kitap → kitapta*.\n",
       "audio": [
        "aud.own.fistikci_sahap"
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "examples",
       "title": "Step by step",
       "body": "Two questions, every time: **which vowel?** then **which consonant?**\n\nPlural first, then the location: **ev·ler·de** \"in the houses\".\n",
       "audio": [
        "aud.own.L10_worked_examples"
       ],
       "interactive": {
        "component": "suffix_steps",
        "params": {
         "words": [
          "w.oda",
          "w.ev",
          "w.dolap",
          "w.otobüs"
         ],
         "suffix": "sfx.loc"
        }
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "rule",
       "title": "Where?",
       "body": "**Nerede?** \"Where?\" — *Kitap nerede? — Kitap çantada.*\n**burada** \"here\" · **orada** \"there\" (they already contain -da: bura·da, ora·da)\n",
       "sentences": [
        "s.L10.003",
        "s.L10.004"
       ]
      }
     ],
     "items": [
      {
       "id": "L10.learn.01",
       "type": "pick_suffix",
       "grammar": [
        "g.L10.loc"
       ],
       "pattern": "g.L10.loc.after_vowel",
       "base": "w.masa",
       "suffix": "sfx.loc",
       "options": [
        "da",
        "de",
        "ta",
        "te"
       ],
       "answer": "da",
